    `the new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies` IS TRUE
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is not in paid work` IS FALSE
    `day on which the claimant ceased paid work` IS YMD 2024 5 1
    `last day of the previous award` IS YMD 2024 4 1
    `date on which the claim is made` IS YMD 2024 6 1
    `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for the delay in making the claim` IS FALSE
    `number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it` IS 7
`reclaim outside a regulation 21(3C) case` MEANS `Reclaim after loss of employment` WITH
    `the new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies` IS FALSE
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is not in paid work` IS TRUE
    `day on which the claimant ceased paid work` IS YMD 2024 5 1
    `last day of the previous award` IS YMD 2024 4 1
    `date on which the claim is made` IS YMD 2024 6 1
    `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for the delay in making the claim` IS FALSE
    `number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it` IS 7
`reclaim that ceased work on 20 May 2024 with 14 days allowed` MEANS `Reclaim after loss of employment` WITH
    `the new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies` IS TRUE
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is not in paid work` IS TRUE
    `day on which the claimant ceased paid work` IS YMD 2024 5 20
    `last day of the previous award` IS YMD 2024 4 1
    `date on which the claim is made` IS YMD 2024 6 1
    `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for the delay in making the claim` IS TRUE
    `number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it` IS 14
`reclaim that ceased work on 18 May 2024 with 14 days allowed` MEANS `Reclaim after loss of employment` WITH
    `the new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies` IS TRUE
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is not in paid work` IS TRUE
    `day on which the claimant ceased paid work` IS YMD 2024 5 18
    `last day of the previous award` IS YMD 2024 4 1
    `date on which the claim is made` IS YMD 2024 6 1
    `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for the delay in making the claim` IS TRUE
    `number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it` IS 14
`reclaim with a shorter period than 7 days allowed` MEANS `Reclaim after loss of employment` WITH
    `the new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies` IS TRUE
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is not in paid work` IS TRUE
    `day on which the claimant ceased paid work` IS YMD 2024 5 26
    `last day of the previous award` IS YMD 2024 4 1
    `date on which the claim is made` IS YMD 2024 6 1
    `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for the delay in making the claim` IS TRUE
    `number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it` IS 3
-- (1)(b): ceasing work 8 days before the claim (25 May) falls outside the 7 days ending with 1 June (26 May to 1 June).
#ASSERT `reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim that ceased work on 1 May 2024`
#ASSERT `reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim that ceased work on 25 May 2024`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim that ceased work on 26 May 2024`)
-- "since the previous award ended": ceasing on its last day is not since it ended; the next day is.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim that ceased work on the day the previous award ended`)
#ASSERT `reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim that ceased work the day after the previous award ended`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim in paid work`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim outside a regulation 21(3C) case`)
-- (3) extended to 14 days: 20 May is inside the 14 days ending 1 June (19 May to 1 June); 18 May is outside.
#ASSERT `reg 22A(3) — the number of days ending with the day of the claim` `reclaim that ceased work on 1 May 2024` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `reg 22A(3) — the number of days ending with the day of the claim` `reclaim that ceased work on 20 May 2024 with 14 days allowed` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `reg 22A(3) — the number of days ending with the day of the claim` `reclaim with a shorter period than 7 days allowed` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim that ceased work on 20 May 2024 with 14 days allowed`)
#ASSERT `reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim that ceased work on 18 May 2024 with 14 days allowed`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `reclaim with a shorter period than 7 days allowed`)
-- (2): N from the claim date (1 June) to the last day of the assessment period (14 June), both counted.
#ASSERT `reg 22A(2) — the number of days from the claim to the end of the assessment period` (YMD 2024 6 1) (YMD 2024 6 14) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `reg 22A(2) — the number of days from the claim to the end of the assessment period` (YMD 2024 6 14) (YMD 2024 6 14) EQUALS 1
-- Across a month end: 20 to 30 June is 11 days and 1 to 19 July is 19, so 30; and 20 to 31 January is 12, 1 to 29 February (2024 is a leap year) is 29, and 1 to 19 March is 19, so 60.
#ASSERT `reg 22A(2) — the number of days from the claim to the end of the assessment period` (YMD 2024 6 20) (YMD 2024 7 19) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `reg 22A(2) — the number of days from the claim to the end of the assessment period` (YMD 2024 1 20) (YMD 2024 3 19) EQUALS 60
-- The formula is not in the deposited text: not covered.
#ASSERT `reg 22A(2) — the reduced amount` 400 14 EQUALS NOTHING
